  "summary": "Results inbox worked under RBC-INBOX-01, RBC-LAB-03 and RBC-RAD-05. Five new results arrived while I worked and I handled them too. Two of them changed decisions I had already made, so I corrected those. One item is still open on purpose and one was handed to RN triage.\n\nORIGINAL 9 ITEMS\n- pt-0016 Ondricka, TSH: normal. Closed.\n- pt-0016 Ondricka, K 6.3: the lab corrected it to 4.4 (normal). Acted on the corrected value and closed with no action.\n- pt-0007 Parisian, preliminary CTA chest (5 mm RUL nodule): the final report (dr-00084) says it is a vessel, with no nodule and no PE. Closed as no follow-up needed under RBC-RAD-05.\n- pt-0007 Parisian, BMP 10-22: kidney injury (AKI). Creatinine went from 0.98 to 1.64 in about 35 h. Ordered an urgent BMP for 10-23 to 10-26, put naproxen on hold (he was also sent home from the ED on ibuprofen), sent an urgent patient message and wrote a note.\n- pt-0065 Nowicki, Lakeshore lung-screening addendum (Lung-RADS 4A): the fax is for a different patient. Its DOB (1951-08-04), MRN (4471-20) and exam date don't match our patient. I placed no order and wrote nothing to her chart. I handed the item to RN triage to call Lakeshore so the finding reaches the right patient's clinician, and to remove the fax from her chart.\n- pt-0064 Marchetti, ED BMP 9-26 (creatinine 1.36): no creatinine was on file in the comparison window, so it did not count as AKI. Closed.\n- pt-0033 Whitfield, BMP 10-22 (creatinine 1.31): the 10-21 value of 0.84 was entered in error (another patient's sample), so I didn't use it. Compared with 1.27 on 10-17 it is not AKI. Closed.\n- pt-0008 Brennan, K 6.4 marked hemolyzed: first handled as a likely false high (urgent repeat BMP sr-t0017, patient message, note). Corrected later, see below.\n- pt-0006 Patel, CT urogram: nothing explains the blood in his urine. There was a 4 mm LLL lung nodule, so I ordered a 12-month chest CT with a tracking task, messaged him and wrote a note. Corrected later, see below.\n\nLATE ARRIVALS AND CORRECTIONS\n- pt-0008: the lab withdrew the hemolysis comment, so K 6.4 is real. I switched to the stat plan in RBC-LAB-03 §1: stat BMP today (sr-t0021), stat message to on-call (asking them to call him and to discontinue sr-t0017), a corrected stat message telling him to come in today, and a note. On the medicine review, no potassium-raising drug was safe to hold. Metoprolol was kept because stopping it suddenly is unsafe with his heart disease.\n- pt-0006: a Lakeshore addendum (Lung-RADS 3, new 5 mm RUL nodule) shows he is already in lung cancer screening and the LLL nodule is the same one they follow. I had missed his April screening CT in the record, so the 12-month CT was the wrong rule. Ordered a screening low-dose CT now through 11-14 (sr-t0035) with a tracking task, sent a corrected patient message and wrote a correction note.\n- pt-0033: new urgent-care creatinine 1.78 vs 1.31 earlier the same day, so AKI. Ordered an urgent BMP by 10-26, sent an urgent message and wrote a note. The note flags the hydrochlorothiazide started 10-17 for review.\n- pt-0064: new creatinine 1.48 vs 0.88 on 10-21, so AKI. Ordered an urgent BMP by 10-26, put naproxen on hold, sent an urgent message and wrote a note.\n\nNEEDS YOUR ACTION\n- Two of my orders need cancelling, and I had no tool to cancel orders:\n  - pt-0006: the 12-month chest CT (sr-t0001) and its tracking task (task-t0002). I made you a task (task-t0037) to discontinue them.\n  - pt-0008: the urgent repeat BMP (sr-t0017). I asked on-call to discontinue it.\n- pt-0007: a new chest X-ray (inbox-a0002) is still preliminary (\"possible 7 mm RUL nodule\"). No final report has been issued, so I left it open.\n- pt-0006: Dr. Reyes has an open critical K 6.3 item (task-00002, hemolyzed sample) that the answering service couldn't pass on to the covering clinician. I messaged Dr. Reyes and took no action on it.\n- Your messages queue (7 refill requests) was outside this task, so I didn't touch it.",
